YMX License
===========

YMX is a family of four repositories: YMXS, the specification of a tune;
YMXR, a player of one for the Atari ST; DTX, the table format under that
player; and ST4, the compression under DTX. This repository contains one
document, README.md, which defines how they fit together, and AGENTS.md,
the house style it is written to.

1. THIS DOCUMENT. README.md, AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md and this file are
   Copyright (c) 2026 Robbert van Dalen. Quote and cite them freely,
   naming YMX as the source.

2. THE FOUR FORMATS are licensed in the repositories that define them,
   each under the LICENSE there:

   * YMXS   https://github.com/odipar/YMXS
   * YMXR   https://github.com/odipar/YMXR
   * DTX    https://github.com/odipar/DTX
   * ST4    https://github.com/odipar/ST4

   Each may be implemented freely, and each sets the same condition:
   your documentation indicates somehow that you have used it. ST4 adds
   a BSD 3-Clause License for its compressor, which a DTX2 column is
   packed with.

3. THE HISTORY. Up to commit 0cab58a this repository contained the YMX
   format, its specification, the 68000 players, the packer and the
   combiners in Java, C# and Go, and the test rigs. A checkout of one of
   those commits includes the LICENSE of that commit, and that LICENSE
   covers the files in it: the BSD 3-Clause License for the ST4
   compressor derived from Einar Saukas' ZX1, the free-use condition for
   the decompressors, players and tools, and the ST-Sound notices for the
   LHA depacker. YMXR, DTX and ST4 contain the successors of those files
   under the same terms.

Attribution
-----------

* YMX and this document are Copyright (c) 2026 Robbert van Dalen; written
  by Claude (Anthropic's Claude Code) under Robbert van Dalen's direction,
  as were the format, the players and the tools in this repository's
  history.
* The ZX1 data compression format and algorithm was designed and
  implemented by Einar Saukas (Copyright (c) 2021), with thanks to
  introspec/spke. ST4 derives from it through ST1
  (https://github.com/odipar/ST1).
* The YM5 and YM6 register-dump formats are by Arnaud Carré
  (Leonard/Oxygene). The LHA depacker that opens a distributed .ym file is
  a port of the LZH code of his ST-Sound library, itself based on LZH code
  by Haruhiko Okumura (1991) and Kerwin F. Medina (1996).
* The player was inspired by Steven Tattersall's MinYMiser.
* SNDH is the Atari ST scene's shared music container; the SNDH files YMXR
  builds follow revision 2.2 of its file structure.
